    "html": "<p>The views icon sits with the board&#39;s own controls, after the outline toggle and before search. It opens\n<a href=\"target:ui:views-layer\">the views layer</a> on the view you were last reading, or on the first one if this is\nyour first visit, and even with no views at all, so that the layer can make one.</p>\n<p>A saved view is a <em>configuration</em>, not a snapshot: the words, scope, chips and pinned cards that select\nsomething, plus the shape it is read in. Nothing is copied out of the document, so editing a card in a\ntable edits the card, and a view somebody else changes redraws for you while you are reading it.</p>\n<p>The rail on the left is every saved view with a live thumbnail. <strong>New view</strong> starts one, and it stays a\nlocal draft until you press <strong>Create</strong>, because until then there is nothing to share.</p>\n<p>To put a view on the board itself, read <a href=\"target:ui:views-projection-bar\">projections</a>: any view can be cast\nover the canvas, outlining what it selects and fading the rest.</p>\n",
    "text": "The views icon sits with the board's own controls, after the outline toggle and before search. It opens the views layer on the view you were last reading, or on the first one if this is your first visit, and even with no views at all, so that the layer can make one. A saved view is a configuration , not a snapshot: the words, scope, chips and pinned cards that select something, plus the shape it is read in. Nothing is copied out of the document, so editing a card in a table edits the card, and a view somebody else changes redraws for you while you are reading it. The rail on the left is every saved view with a live thumbnail. New view starts one, and it stays a local draft until you press Create , because until then there is nothing to share. To put a view on the board itself, read projections : any view can be cast over the canvas, outlining what it selects and fading the rest."
